{"repositoryId":840560677,"availability":"available","full":"CreateJGN/sleeter-react-django","name":"sleeter-react-django","description":"Self-hostable web app for isolating the vocal, accompaniment, bass, and drums of any song. Supports Spleeter, D3Net, Demucs, Tasnet, X-UMX. Built with React and Django.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2024-08-10T02:43:36Z","updated":"2026-10-13T04:45:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://jeffreyca.github.io/spleeter-web/","topics":["d3net","demucs","django","react","rossnet-open-unmix","source-separation","spleeter","tasnet","x-umx"],"demo":"https://jeffreyca.github.io/spleeter-web/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.577Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.577Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.577Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.577Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Spleeter Web is a web application for isolating or removing the vocal, accompaniment, bass, and/or drum components of any song. For example, you can use it to isolate the vocals of a track, or you can use it remove the vocals to get an instrumental version of a song.","It supports a number of different source separation models: Spleeter (4stems-model and 5stems-model), Demucs, CrossNet-Open-Unmix, and D3Net.","The app uses Django for the backend API and React for the frontend. Celery is used for the task queue. Docker images are available, including ones with GPU support."],"features":["Supports Spleeter, Demucs, CrossNet-Open-Unmix (X-UMX), and D3Net source separation models","Dynamic Mixes let you export and play back in realtime your own custom mix of the different components","Import tracks by uploading an audio file or by a YouTube link","Supports lossy (MP3) and lossless (FLAC, WAV) output formats","Persistent audio library with ability to stream and download your source tracks and mixes"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CreateJGN/sleeter-react-django/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"e7caae12c84d324eee3f91f401c657f6ed672904ad907f850e08e6735df57f17","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.707Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.707Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Spleeter Web is a web application for isolating or removing the vocal, accompaniment, bass, and/or drum components of any song. For example, you can use it to isolate the vocals of a track, or you can use it remove the vocals to get an instrumental version of a song.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CreateJGN/sleeter-react-django/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"(Optional) Set the YouTube Data API key (for YouTube search functionality):","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CreateJGN/sleeter-react-django/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e7caae12c84d324eee3f91f401c657f6ed672904ad907f850e08e6735df57f17","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CreateJGN/sleeter-react-django/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.707Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-13T04:45:34Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CreateJGN/sleeter-react-django/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:35.707Z","hash":"e7caae12c84d324eee3f91f401c657f6ed672904ad907f850e08e6735df57f17","originalBytes":18871,"storedBytes":18871,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["set","storage","spleeter-web","docker","aws","default","file","azure","celery","env","separation","youtube","used","api","source","when","django","key","settings","gpu","using","build","host","port","spleeter","install","docker-compose","domain","web","access","docker-compose.prod.yml","environment","fast","name","queue","slow","tasks","variables","worker","d3net","docker-compose.prod.selfhost.yml","docker-compose.yml","media","nginx","only.","optional","python","run","start","accoun